# Every variable the console reads, with what it is for.
# Copy to .env.local for local work.
#
# READ THIS FIRST. Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed value into the JavaScript bundle as
# plain text. There is no such thing as a secret in this file: whatever is written here is
# readable by anyone who can open the console. That is not a weakness to work around, it
# is why the realm makes brain-console a public client with PKCE rather than giving it a
# client secret it could not keep.
#
# The client id is deliberately NOT here. It is a constant in src/auth/constants.ts,
# because a client id an operator can change is a client id that can be pointed at a
# different Keycloak client with different flow settings, and the console cannot tell the
# difference. See that file.

# --- the API ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A path, not a URL, because the console is served from the same origin as the API: the
# realm registers https://brain.example.invalid/auth/callback for this client, and the
# API lives under /api/v1 on that same host. `npm run dev` proxies this path to the
# backend so development uses the same-origin shape the deployment uses.
#
# Set a full origin here only if a deployment really does split the two, and then also set
# BRAIN_CORS_ORIGINS on the API and add the console origin to webOrigins in the realm.
# Two changes, in two systems, neither of which fails loudly on its own.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# --- identity --------------------------------------------------------------
# The realm's issuer URL, exactly as Keycloak publishes it, with no trailing slash. The
# console appends /.well-known/openid-configuration to it and reads the endpoints from
# there rather than guessing Keycloak's URL shapes.
#
# This must be the same issuer the API expects. brain.identity.oidc compares `iss` by
# exact string equality and refuses anything else, so a trailing slash or a host that
# differs by a redirect presents as every token being rejected after a successful sign-in.
VITE_KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=https://keycloak.example.invalid/realms/brain

# --- development only ------------------------------------------------------
# Where `npm run dev` proxies /api. Never inlined into the bundle: this one has no VITE_
# prefix on purpose, and is read by vite.config.ts in the Node process.
DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000
